BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:23rd Annual Heirloom Apple Day
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTSTAMP:20261011T164043Z
UID:b97f86ac1aa250a7591b03f02f762d@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:It's almost time once again for our biggest event of the year 
 - Heirloom Apple Day! Join us from 10am-5pm on Sunday\, Oct 11\, for a cel
 ebration of apples of all shapes\, colors\, tastes\, and their histories. 
 This family friendly event will once again include all day tastings\, our 
 famous heirloom apple display\, and oodles of opportunities to leave with 
 lots of apples. Plus live music\, food trucks\, kids activities (face pain
 ting\, pumpkin painting\, yard games)\, The Stone Trust Stone Wall Park\, 
 and local vendors and nonprofits. Returning this year is the incredible "a
 pple explorer" John Bunker. An expert on American apples and their history
 \, he is one of the founders of the mail-order nursery Fedco Trees\, a div
 ision of the cooperative Fedco Seeds. For most of his life\, Bunker has wo
 rked to preserve rare old apple varieties from across Maine and the New En
 gland region. In 2012\, he founded the Maine Heritage Orchard in Unity\, M
 e.\, a ten-acre preservation educational orchard of Maine's historic apple
  and pear varieties. We're also pleased to welcome historian Todd Little-S
 iebold. Todd is a professor of history at the College of the Atlantic in B
 ar Harbor\, Maine. He teaches classes on a wide range of topics\, includin
 g one on the history of apples. His class “The Cider Project” was a ye
 ar-long experiment in teaching the history and techniques of making hard c
 ider. He has spent the last fifteen years tracking down\, researching\, an
 d helping to preserve heirloom apples in downeast Maine. He has collaborat
 ed with the Maine Heritage Orchard since its inception in 2014 to build it
 s current collection of 400 rare and historic cultivars. Don't miss this o
 ne day only FREE to attend event. If you come to Scott Farm only once this
  year\, this is the day to do it!\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Scott Farm Orchard\, 707 Kipling Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/23rd-annua
 l-heirloom-apple-day-01-10-2026-17-07-14
END:VEVENT
