BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roger Clark Miller and Michael Tarbox at Stage 33 Live
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTSTAMP:20261011T164043Z
UID:d78210a67fa309fc751d0f48d1e46e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Roger Clark Miller is the founding guitarist of the highly inf
 luential rock band Mission of Burma\, and has performed nationally and int
 ernationally as a solo artist and leading a variety of bands and ensembles
 . He’s also a respected writer\, music historian\, and more. The songs o
 n his new album\, “The Green Man”\, have a different feel from anythin
 g he’s done previously\, evolving out of a series of “Unplugged from a
  Band” shows. This record has been a long time coming\, and he'll be per
 forming selections solo with just his guitar\, voice\, and a looper. Micha
 el Tarbox writes songs anchored in rock ‘n’ roll\, backwater blues\, h
 illbilly music\, and country — rough-hewn\, immediate\, and hard-won. Hi
 s songs have been used in the television shows Sons of Anarchy and Superna
 tural. “My inspirations are musicians from a world that’s vanished. I 
 let them guide me\, but my goal is to create something new\,” he says. T
 arbox began his career with The Tarbox Ramblers\, a hard-hitting quartet t
 hat released well-received albums on Rounder and played countless shows th
 roughout the U.S. and Canada. Roger Clark Miller celebrates his new album
 \, “The Green Man”\, in a 3:00 matinee concert on Sunday\, October 11 
 at Stage 33 Live in Bellows Falls\, Vermont. At Roger's request\, Michael 
 Tarbox shares the bill. Tickets are $20 in advance through stage33live.com
 \, or at the door as available. Advance tickets guarantee entry. Only 40 t
 ickets will be sold. Advance sales will close at midnight the day before t
 he show\, or when 40 tickets are sold. Ticket proceeds go entirely to the 
 performers. The performances will be recorded and filmed. Stage 33 Live is
  a casual and intimate industrial-rustic listening room in a former factor
 y hosting local\, regional\, and national performances and presentations o
 f original material. No bar or kitchen\, the stage is the mission\; coffee
  / soda / juice / water and weird snacks available by donation. More infor
 mation about the nonprofit\, all-volunteer project\, and this and other up
 coming events\, online at stage33live.com Stage 33 Live gratefully acknowl
 edges the help of so many individuals without whom none of this would be a
 ble to happen\, and institutional support this season from The Island Corp
 oration\, WOOL-FM\, Guilford Sound\, and the Rockingham Arts & Museum Proj
 ect to help fund improvements and maintenance\, and generally smooth out a
  lot of the rough edges. Stage 33 Live is a 501(c)3 nonprofit organization
 \, and all donations are deductible to the fullest extent. Volunteers run 
 the thing from stem to stern.\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Stage 33 Live\, 33 Bridge Street\, Bellows Falls VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/roger-clar
 k-miller-and-michael-tarbox-at-stage-33-live-23-09-2026-08-01-54
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What the Constitution Means to Me
DTSTART:20261011T193000
DTEND:20261011T213000
DTSTAMP:20261011T164043Z
UID:6af1acacb2af0e79a0f4e3d8e99dda@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:This extraordinary\, stimulating OBIE-Award-Winning play based
  on a true story\, is the final show of Lost Nation Theater’s 2026 Seaso
 n. At 15\, playwright Heidi Schreck earned her college tuition by winning 
 debate competitions about the Constitution. In her hilarious\, hopeful\, a
 nd achingly human play based on those experiences\, she documents how this
  founding document of our country informed and shaped the women in her fam
 ily through four generations. A boundary-breaking exploration that breathe
 s new life into our Constitution. Masks are encouraged\, not required. (LN
 T’s State of the Art Bio-Defense Air Purification “Synexis” System i
 s keeping everyone as safe as possible.) WHEN: Wednesdays-Sundays\, Octobe
 r 1-October 11\, 2026 WHERE: Lost Nation Theater\, 39 Main St\, Montpelier
 \, VT 05602 2pm Matinees Sundays\, plus Saturday October 10. COST: $15 - $
 45\, depending on day/type of ticket. Center reserved guarantee seats avai
 lable for additional fee. INFO & TICKETS: WWW.LOSTNATIONTHEATER.ORG Montpe
 lier City Hall's elevator is finally open and in operation\, making our th
 eater accessible once more!! And LNT is also Air Conditioned! Please\, ind
 icate access needs when placing your order. SPONSORS: The City of Montpeli
 er\, Vermont Mutual Insurance Co\, Random Acts of Kindness Fund\, Eternity
 \, The Point!-FM\, Estate of Ted Richards\, The Mary Shriver Fund of the A
 lan Weiss Estate ABOUT LNT: Lost Nation Theater winner “Theater of the D
 ecade” – Broadway World (2020)\; “Best of New England”\, Yankee Ma
 gazine\, was named “One of the Best regional theaters in America” by t
 he New York Drama League\, “Outstanding Achievement Award” from the Ne
 w England Theatre Conference\; and has won the People’s Choice awards fr
 om both Seven Days and The Times Argus for Best Theater.\n\nSources: Vermo
 nt Public
LOCATION:Lost Nation Theater\, 39 Main St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/what-the-c
 onstitution-means-to-me-01-09-2026-13-35-36
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:19th Annual LEGO Contest & Exhibit
DTSTART:20261012T100000
DTEND:20261012T160000
DTSTAMP:20261011T164043Z
UID:b7b5b9f0356a8abc96f65558fcdc00@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Build your very own LEGO creation and display it at BMAC! Desi
 gn and build an original LEGO structure according to contest guidelines av
 ailable below\, or just drop by and check out the fantastic submissions on
  display October 8-12\, 10-4. New this year: Submit your LEGO stop-motion 
 animation videos\, and they will play during the exhibit. Details and guid
 elines available brattleboromuseum.org Prizes for Creativity and Craftsman
 ship will be awarded in six age groups: * Preschool-K * Grades 1-3 * Grade
 s 4-6 * Grades 7-12 * Adult * Adult/Child collaboration Additionally\, one
  spectacular submission will be designated Best in Show. Special prizes wi
 ll be awarded in the following categories: * Best Vehicle\, sponsored by B
 rattleboro Subaru * Best Home or Building\, sponsored by Foard Panel * Bes
 t Use of Moving Parts\, sponsored by Global Precision * Best Use of Light 
 or Color\, sponsored by Chroma Winners of Best in Show and the four specia
 l categories will receive $100 gift cards to the LEGO Store. All other win
 ners will receive gift cards to A2Z Science & Toys in Northampton\, Mass. 
 All prizes will be announced at an Awards Ceremony at the museum on Thursd
 ay\, October 8\, at 5:30 p.m. Entries will be on display at the museum Thu
 rsday October 8 through Monday October 12. Admission is pay as you wish. N
 OTE: Entries must be delivered to the Brattleboro Museum & Art Center on T
 uesday\, October 6\, between 4 and 6 p.m. See the entry form at the link a
 bove for more information. The entry form and $5 entry fee must be submitt
 ed in advance\, before you drop off your work. RELATED EVENTS October 8\, 
 Thursday\, 5:30 p.m. — 19th Annual LEGO Exhibit & Contest Awards Ceremon
 y\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Brattleboro Museum & Art Center\, 10 Vernon Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/19th-annua
 l-lego-contest-amp-exhibit-05-10-2026-11-33-41
END:VEVENT
